Dear Dr. Seitz:

	Enclosed please find an extended abstract of the paper
"Design of LISP-based Processors", by myself and Gerald Jay
Sussman, which Lynn Conway recommended we submit to the
conference on VLSI Architecture, Design, and Fabrication
to be held at Caltech on 22-24 January 1979.

	We apologize for the length of the abstract; if we had
had more lead time to work on it, it would have been much shorter!
We will try to tighten it up somewhat in the next month as
it grows into a full paper, and give more space to describing
the particular VLSI design.  For now we were concerned primarily
with presenting the general architectural idea, which takes a
fair amount of background for an audience unfamiliar with LISP.

	We look forward to hearing from you, and hope this
contribution will be suitable for the conference.

				Yours,


				Guy L. Steele Jr.
